{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the birds he did not divide.</b> Why did he divide the animals and not the birds? Because the animals allude to idolaters, who are likened to beasts, as it is said (Psalms 22:13): ״סבבוני פרים״, and it is written (Daniel 8:20): ״האיל אשר ראית״, and it is written there: ״והצפיר השעיר״, and they are destined to perish; but Israel is likened to a dove, as it is said (Song of Songs 5:2): ״יונתי תמתי״, and it is written (Song of Songs 2:14): ״יונתי בחגוי הסלע״, and Israel shall endure forever; therefore he did not divide the birds."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:31.595135557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}